  "query_preview": "..\n\nUpper ridge will build into the region over the next few days,\nbefore flattening outh by midweek. Northwest flow will then\nprevail into next weekend.\n\nAt the surface, high pressure will be sliding across the northern\nplains, for warming temperatures through Monday. A dry cold front\nwill drop through the flow on Tuesday for a slight cool down for\nmidweek. \n\nThe next potential for rain will be next weekend with a trough\nmoving into the northern Rockies. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nNo changes were made from the NBM. Confidence for rain chances are\nlow, especially into the late week period.\n\nRAE/FINDLEY",
